OL,3,ABurnham suggests stocking up on tinned
OL,4,Afood and bottled water
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe prime minister has advised people
OL,7,Fto stock up on tinned food and bottled
OL,8,Fwater in order to be prepared for
OL,9,Femergencies.
OL,11,FWith storms battering the UK, and in
OL,12,Fthe wake of online disruption caused by
OL,13,Fa major security flaw, Andy Burnham
OL,14,Fsaid "unexpected events seem to be
OL,15,Fbecoming more and more common".
OL,17,FThe government has drawn up
OL,18,Frecommendations for households to have
OL,19,Fthree days' worth of bottled water and
OL,20,Ftinned food to deal with a crisis such
OL,21,Fas a war, an online attack or a natural
OL,22,Fdisaster.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/40
